+## Patch 9: staged tensor binding boundary
+
+Patch 9 adds two private runtime components without changing public loader behavior:
+
+- `inkling_bind.[ch]` maps canonical `inkling.*` tensor names into the verified
+  model/layer weight structures. Every required tensor must occur exactly once
+  with the exact config-derived rank and shape. Routed experts remain callback
+  supplied and are not made resident by the binder.
+- `inkling_stage_reader.[ch]` opens converter-internal trunk tensor artifacts and
+  BF16 expert banks. It validates magic, version, dtype, rank, shape, canonical
+  name CRC, record identity, offsets, payload geometry, and optional CRC32 before
+  exposing an F32 row or expert.
+
+These files deliberately consume staging formats, not `manifest.json` or WEXP.
+They establish the byte-to-runtime boundary while the public loader continues to
+return unsupported for Inkling. A complete private directory opener and synthetic
+open-to-logits parity remain the next milestone.
